# valet-key per-profile config-dir overrides. Copy to ~/.config/valet-key/dirs
# and edit.
#
# Lines: <agent> <profile> <dir>. When <agent> runs in <profile>, valet-key
# points
# it at <dir> instead of the adapter's default (<base> for the default profile,
# <base>-<profile> otherwise). A leading ~ expands to $HOME. Blank lines and
# lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# Use it for a config dir that must live at a specific path (a sealed location),
# or for a tool whose env var points at a HOME rather than a config dir -- e.g.
# gemini's GEMINI_CLI_HOME, where the default <base>-<profile> naming would be
# an awkward $HOME sibling.
#
# Example: pin the work gemini home to a dedicated directory.
#
#   gemini  work  ~/.config/gemini-work
